<% const inventory = getCredentialInventory(); const ownerId = typeof req.query?.owner === 'string' ? req.query.owner : req.path === '/admin/certs/regenerate' && typeof req.body?.owner === 'string' ? req.body.owner : '';  const selectedOwner = inventory.owners.find(owner => owner.id === ownerId); const rows = ownerId ? inventory.rows.filter(row => row.owner.id === ownerId) : inventory.rows; %>
<div class="admin-toolbar">
<form method="get" action="<%= basePath %>/admin" class="admin-security-target"><input type="hidden" name="section" value="certificates"><% if (state.source) { %><input type="hidden" name="source" value="<%= state.source %>"><% } %>
<label for="certificate-owner" data-help-key="admin.cert-owner">Owner</label><select id="certificate-owner" name="owner" class="form-select" data-help-key="admin.cert-owner"><option value="">All owners</option><% inventory.owners.forEach(owner => { %><option value="<%= owner.id %>" <%= owner.id === ownerId ? 'selected' : '' %>><%= owner.name %> · <%= owner.id %></option><% }) %></select>
<button class="btn btn-outline-primary" data-help-key="admin.cert-owner">Show owner</button></form>
<button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-primary" data-admin-toggle="certificate-renewal" aria-expanded="<%= options.renewalReview ? 'true' : 'false' %>" aria-controls="certificate-renewal" data-help-key="admin.cert-regenerate">How to renew certificates</button>
<a class="btn btn-outline-secondary" href="<%= shell.address(basePath, 'certificates', state.source) %><%= ownerId ? '&owner=' + encodeURIComponent(ownerId) : '' %>" data-help-key="admin.cert-refresh">Refresh</a></div>
<p>Owner filtering affects this inventory only. Renewal instructions and credential exports describe their team-wide scope.</p>
<p data-help-key="admin.certificates">Files checked <%= inventory.checkedAt %> · saved revision <%= inventory.revision %>. Registration checks use the current PCM client resolver. Listener adoption is unknown; files on disk do not prove a running listener loaded them.</p>
<% if (ownerId && !selectedOwner) { %><p class="alert alert-warning" role="alert">This credential owner is no longer configured. Choose a current owner; no replacement was selected.</p><% } %>
<% if (selectedOwner?.context?.section === 'sources') { %><p><a class="btn btn-outline-primary" href="<%= shell.address(basePath, 'sources', selectedOwner.context.source, 'credentials') %>" data-help-key="admin.source-credentials">Open source credentials</a></p><% } %>
<section id="certificate-renewal" class="card" aria-label="Controlled certificate renewal" <%= options.renewalReview ? '' : 'hidden' %>><div class="card-body"><div class="admin-toolbar"><h3 data-help-key="admin.cert-regenerate">Renew team-managed certificates</h3><button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary" data-admin-dismiss="certificate-renewal" data-help-key="admin.cert-regenerate">Close instructions</button></div>
<p role="status">Certificate renewal requires controlled listener recreation. No credentials were changed.</p>
<p>Renew registered team-owned leaves under the existing issuer. Root authorities, participant-owned uploads, unknown ownership and negative-test issuers stay protected. Preview validates current material; an inventory alone is not a renewal readiness result.</p>
<ol><li>On the local operator host, preview the exact selected team with <code>node pcm-connectathon/scripts/rotate-team-certificates.js --team-id &lt;team-id&gt; --teams-root &lt;local-teams-root&gt;</code>.</li><li>Review affected roles and preserved material. Plan an interruption and protect the private config, environment and credential backup.</li><li>Run the same reviewed command with <code>--apply</code>. The controlled workflow prepares and validates all leaves, stops only this team without deleting volumes, creates a private backup, publishes the complete graph and recreates listeners.</li><li>Verify listener health, actual registrations and ordinary source/app requests. Failed recreation restores old material only after partial listeners stop; failed cleanup/restoration leaves an uncertain state requiring operator recovery.</li></ol>
<p>Leaf renewal retains private keys by default. Add <code>--rotate-keys</code> only for deliberate key replacement; registered source/app IDs stay fixed. Renewed transport fingerprints can invalidate issued token correlation even with the same key. Replaced assertion keys change signing key IDs. Restart affected tests and obtain fresh tokens; neither action extends Consent, Contract or first-use authority. Explicit private JWT key IDs may block rotation before listeners stop.</p>
<% if (options.renewalReview) { %><details><summary data-help-key="common.details">Configured renewal roles and preserved owners</summary><pre><%= JSON.stringify(options.renewalReview, null, 2) %></pre></details><% } %>
<a class="btn btn-outline-primary" href="<%= shell.address(basePath, 'certificates', state.source) + (ownerId ? '&owner=' + encodeURIComponent(ownerId) : '') %>" data-help-key="common.nav-admin">Back to Certificates</a></div></section>
<section aria-label="Credential role inventory" data-credential-inventory>
<% rows.forEach(row => { %><article class="card" data-credential-row><div class="card-body">
<h3><%= row.owner.name %> · <%= row.role %></h3><p><%= row.owner.kind %> · <code><%= row.owner.id %></code><% if (row.owner.clientId) { %> · client <code><%= row.owner.clientId %></code><% } %> · <%= row.owner.enabled ? 'Enabled configuration' : 'Disabled configuration' %><% if (row.owner.ownership) { %> · credential ownership: <%= row.owner.ownership %><% } %></p>
<dl class="admin-certificate-facts" data-help-key="admin.certificates"><div><dt>Algorithm / profile</dt><dd><%= row.algorithm %> · <%= row.profile %></dd></div><div><dt>Validity</dt><dd><%= row.validity %> · <%= row.validFrom %> to <%= row.validTo %></dd></div><div><dt>Issuer</dt><dd><%= row.issuer %></dd></div><div><dt>File checks</dt><dd><%= row.material %></dd></div><div><dt>Registration</dt><dd><%= row.registration %></dd></div><div><dt>Loaded by listener</dt><dd><%= row.loaded %></dd></div></dl>
<% if (row.fingerprint && row.owner.kind !== 'Unknown owner' && !row.owner.id.startsWith('file:')) { %><a class="btn btn-outline-primary" data-help-key="admin.cert-public-download" href="<%= basePath %>/admin/certs/certificate?owner=<%= encodeURIComponent(row.owner.id) %>&amp;role=<%= encodeURIComponent(row.role) %>&amp;fingerprint=<%= encodeURIComponent(row.fingerprint) %>">Download certificate</a><% } else { %><p>Certificate-only download unavailable: <%= row.fingerprint ? 'no registered owner for this file' : row.material %>.</p><% } %>
<% if (row.owner.context?.section === 'sources') { %><a class="btn btn-outline-primary" href="<%= shell.address(basePath, 'sources', row.owner.context.source, 'credentials') %>" data-help-key="admin.source-credentials">Open source credentials</a><% } else if (row.owner.context?.section === 'apps') { %><a class="btn btn-outline-primary" href="<%= shell.address(basePath, 'apps', state.source) %>#provider-<%= encodeURIComponent(row.owner.context.providerRole) %>" data-help-key="admin.apps-inventory">Open app registration</a><% } %>
<details><summary data-help-key="admin.cert-fingerprint">Fingerprint and file location</summary><p>File: <code><%= row.file %></code></p><% if (row.fingerprint) { %><div data-endpoint><code tabindex="0" data-exact-address><%= row.fingerprint %></code><button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary" data-copy-address data-copy-label="Fingerprint" data-help-key="admin.cert-fingerprint" aria-label="Copy fingerprint for <%= row.owner.name %> <%= row.role %>">Copy fingerprint</button><span role="status" data-copy-status></span></div><% } else { %><p>Fingerprint unavailable: certificate missing or invalid.</p><% } %></details>
</div></article><% }) %>
<% if (!rows.length) { %><p>No credential roles for this owner.</p><% } %></section>
<section class="card"><div class="card-body"><h3 data-help-key="admin.cert-download">Credential export — includes private keys</h3><p>Exports include the current certificate-directory files, private keys and any present CA keys for permitted local portability. They contain secrets. This is not a complete team backup: configuration, environment, clinical databases, Consents and logs are separate.</p>
<div class="admin-source-exports"><a class="btn btn-outline-primary" data-help-key="admin.cert-download" href="<%= basePath %>/admin/certs/download-bundle">Export credentials as JSON</a><a class="btn btn-outline-primary" data-help-key="admin.cert-download" href="<%= basePath %>/admin/certs/download-zip">Export credentials as ZIP</a></div>
<p>Generate or upload custom-source credentials in <a href="<%= shell.address(basePath, 'sources', '', 'onboarding') %>" data-help-key="admin.source-credentials">Source onboarding</a>. Existing SP registration context is in <a href="<%= shell.address(basePath, 'apps', state.source) %>" data-help-key="admin.apps-inventory">Service providers &amp; apps</a>; new SP onboarding remains deferred.</p></div></section>
